# oracle: 27 TIP4P/2005 waters, pair lj/long/tip4p/long cut long (LJ cut at 8.5, Coulomb long) with kspace pppm/tip4p, which reads the M sites from this pair as native PPPMTIP4P::init does through extract, NVE 50 steps
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.4e-12, atoms 2.3e-12; this also covers the cut LJ branch of the pair (flag_lj cut).
# oracle-inputs: w117cf_tip4p_pppm_water.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       w117cf_tip4p_pppm_water.data
pair_style      lj/long/tip4p/long cut long 1 2 1 1 0.1546 8.5
pair_modify     table 0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff      1 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.0 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 55.0 104.52
kspace_style    pppm/tip4p 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   gewald 0.37833912 mesh 12 12 12 order 5
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        1.0
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
